# DEAD FILE — Docker only reads .dockerignore from the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT.
# That used to be this directory (`build: ./backend`), but the fix for the
# missing-protocol/-schemas defect (2026-08-07, see backend/Dockerfile's
# `COPY protocol/` comment) moved the build context to the repo root, so
# this file has been inert since that change — Docker no longer reads it.
#
# The real secret-exclusion rules (backend/.env must never be baked into
# an image layer) now live in the repo-root `.dockerignore`. Edit that
# file, not this one. Left in place rather than deleted only so this note
# is here if anyone goes looking for why the old rules stopped applying.
